# BUILD A PRODUCTION-READY AI LEARNING PLATFORM — MINDFORGE AI

Act as a senior full-stack engineer, AI engineer, UI/UX designer, database architect, security engineer, and product manager. Build a complete, functional, production-quality AI learning platform called **MindForge AI**.

The product is inspired by NotebookLM, Quizlet, and modern AI study tools, but must have its own unique design, identity, and user experience.

**IMPORTANT:** Do not build only a landing page, static prototype, or collection of mock components. Build the complete full-stack application with working authentication, real file processing, AI-powered learning generation, persistent data storage, error handling, and deployment configuration.

Do not stop after generating the initial UI. Implement the backend, connect all features, test the important user flows, and fix errors before considering the project complete.

## 1. Product vision

Users should be able to upload study notes, PDFs, text documents, and other supported files, or provide a publicly accessible video URL. The application should analyze the source material and let users generate whichever learning resources they want.

Core capabilities:
- Upload PDFs, notes, TXT, DOCX, and supported documents.
- Submit publicly accessible YouTube video links and extract available captions or transcripts.
- Summarize long documents into understandable notes.
- Generate AI flashcards with questions and answers.
- Generate MCQ quizzes, true/false questions, short-answer questions, and practice exams.
- Generate topic-wise revision notes, key concepts, definitions, and important questions.
- Provide an interactive AI tutor that answers questions grounded in uploaded sources.
- Display source references and page numbers or video timestamps when available.
- Save study materials, edit generated content, and revisit previous sessions.
- Track quiz scores, learning progress, and flashcard revision history.
- Support multiple languages where the configured AI model supports them.

The application must clearly communicate that generated answers can contain mistakes and should be verified against source material.

## 2. Technology stack

Use a modern, maintainable, full-stack architecture.

Preferred stack:
- Frontend: React, TypeScript, and Vite.
- Styling: Tailwind CSS with shadcn/ui or an equivalent accessible component library.
- Icons: Lucide.
- Backend: Node.js with TypeScript and Express, or a well-supported integrated backend architecture.
- Database: PostgreSQL using Drizzle ORM or Prisma.
- Authentication: secure session-based authentication or a reputable authentication provider.
- AI: an API-based language model with configurable provider and model settings.
- File storage: private object storage when available; otherwise a secure development-compatible storage implementation.
- Validation: Zod or equivalent shared schemas.
- Testing: Vitest and Playwright or equivalent tools.
- Deployment: Replit-compatible configuration with environment variables, persistent storage, and documented setup.

Use the current supported package versions and ensure the project runs within the actual Replit environment. If a preferred technology or service is unavailable, choose a practical compatible alternative rather than leaving unfinished features.

Do not hardcode API keys. Keep all secrets on the server.

