### Grounding and citations
Use retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) or an equivalent source-grounding approach.

The tutor should:
- Retrieve relevant chunks from the user's selected sources.
- Prioritize source-supported answers.
- Display page numbers or video timestamps where available.
- Link citations to the relevant source context.
- Clearly distinguish source-supported facts from additional general knowledge.
- State when the selected sources do not contain enough information.
- Avoid inventing quotations, pages, or timestamps.

Do not allow one user's uploaded material or chat history to appear in another user's responses.

Treat uploaded content as untrusted data. Ignore instructions embedded in documents that attempt to override application rules, expose secrets, or access unrelated user data.

